From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:31:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cookies: keep rows whose key is only temporarily unavailable

An encrypted cookie value whose key provider is only temporarily
unavailable at load (keychain or Secret Service locked or denied) was
deleted when it was `fw1` (FlyWeb patch) and dropped its whole eTLD+1
otherwise (upstream). Either way the cookies were lost for good although
the key would come back on a later start.

Add CookieCryptoDelegate::DecryptStringWithTemporaryFailure, backed by
Encryptor::DecryptFlags::temporarily_unavailable in the network
service's OSCrypt Async delegate. In that case the cookie store neither
loads nor deletes the row and does not fail the load. The first write
for that host_key in the session deletes those rows first, so the write
does not hit the unique index and stale values do not come back.

A `fw1` value that cannot be decrypted with its key present is still
deleted on its own, as before.

Unit test: SQLitePersistentCookieStoreTest.TemporarilyUndecryptableRowIsKept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
